<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Codex Justinianus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Codex Justinianus is the collection of imperial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman laws</a> compiled on the orders of the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a> in the sixth century CE. It formed one part of the larger <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corpus-juris-civilis">Corpus Juris Civilis</a>. It preserved and systematised Roman law within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> and later influenced European legal systems.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/codex-justinianus.jpg" alt="Codex Justinianus" width="320" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghent,_Ghent_University_Library_MS_Bibliotheek_Letteren_en_Wijsbegeerte-Handschriften_0021_fol._24v-25r_Code_of_Justinian.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
